.TH tapectl-volume-list 1  "tapectl-volume-list " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-volume\-list \- List every volume, most recently written first (issue #195)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl volume list\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-status\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List every volume, most recently written first (issue #195).
.PP
Catalog\-only: never opens a drive. Every status is shown by default — ADR\-0011: retired means unfit to WRITE, not unreadable ("a retired volume can still be restored from"), and the dangerous failure for an inventory is a tape you forgot you had. `\-\-status` narrows; nothing is hidden without it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR \fI<STATUS>\fR
Only volumes in this status (blank, initialized, active, full, retired, missing, erased, sealed, quarantined). Every status is shown when omitted
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
